{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-93778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the differential equation $x{y}^{″}+2{x}^{2}{y}^{′}=1,$ what is the associated homogeneous equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-93778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a second-order inhomogeneous ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe associated homogeneous equation is constructed by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\nx{y}^{″}+2{x}^{2}{y}^{′}=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-93778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "56ce1d7afacf04ffe117aed387b464ff993a9df92116057df1336d797455df06"} {"question" "q-93778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-93778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x{y}^{″}+2{x}^{2}{y}^{′}=0"] ["math" "x{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}{y}^{′}=0"] ["math" "x{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}{y}^{′}=1"] ["math" "{y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-93778" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x{y}^{″}+2{x}^{2}{y}^{′}=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-130995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the differential equation ${y}^{″}-6{y}^{′}+5y=9{e}^{2x},$ what is the associated homogeneous equation?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-130995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a second-order inhomogeneous ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe associated homogeneous equation is constructed by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-6{y}^{′}+5y=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-130995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "56ce1d7afacf04ffe117aed387b464ff993a9df92116057df1336d797455df06"} {"question" "q-130995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-130995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{-2x}{y}^{″}-6{y}^{′}+5y=9"] ["math" "{y}^{″}-6{y}^{′}+5y=0"] ["math" "{y}^{″}-6{y}^{′}=0"] ["math" "{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+y=0"] ["math" "{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+y={e}^{2x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-130995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{″}-6{y}^{′}+5y=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-130998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n\n- $5{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,y(0)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=1$\n- ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-{e}^{x}{y}^{′}=0,\\,y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=0$\n- $\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}{y}^{′}={e}^{x},\\,y(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=2$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-130998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$).\n\n- The second system is not an initial value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=1$). This is a **boundary value problem.**\n\n- The third system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$)." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-130998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "56ce1d7afacf04ffe117aed387b464ff993a9df92116057df1336d797455df06"} {"question" "q-130998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-130998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-130998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.$\\,$ The equation $\\,\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+y=0$ is {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}=x$ is {{field-2}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}-xy+4x=0$ is {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-338004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}=x\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=x,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-xy+4x=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-xy=-4x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=-4x,$ which is different from zero." 