0$\n- ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+y=8$\n- $x{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-3y={e}^{x},\\,y(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=4$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-339254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not an initial value problem.  It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=-1$ and $x=2$). This is a **boundary value problem.**\n\n- The second system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$)." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "file_sha256" "590adcdd85f4056afdad3a5b681ee9023ce77efdda2bdc10a1a7cc347ad7d64d"} {"question" "q-339254" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "56ce1d7afacf04ffe117aed387b464ff993a9df92116057df1336d797455df06"} {"question" "q-339254" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072286/state.json" "